  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness 文档资料库",
      "text": "让 PDF 问答有据可查。在 dsh Web 中管理项目文档、检索原文，点击回答中的引用即可查看原页高亮。\n\n[English](README.en.md) · [安装](#安装) · [配置](docs/configuration.md) · [更新记录](CHANGELOG.md)\n\n*示例手册的引用导航实拍；截图中的对话使用本地协议测试模型。*"
    },
    {
      "section": "能做什么",
      "text": "- **项目资料库**：PDF 加入一次，同项目会话复用；每个会话单独勾选检索范围。\n- **后台索引**：查看文字覆盖、视觉页卡和建立过程，支持停止与续建。\n- **原页证据**：检索候选、补读邻页，再将回答中的引用连接到原 PDF。\n- **图表读页**：复用 dsh 当前视觉模型查看页面图像，处理图表和低文本页面。\n- **可展开的过程**：原生工具卡片显示候选页、摘录、耗时和运行状态。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "需要 dsh Web、Node.js 22.19+（22 系列）或 24+，以及 Python 3.10+（含 venv）。已验证宿主为 `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.3-alpha.2`，运行环境为 macOS arm64。\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-document-evidence@beta\ndsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-document-evidence-setup\ndsh web\n```\n\n已运行的 dsh 需要重启。安装辅助程序创建插件专用 Python 环境并安装 PyMuPDF。插件使用 dsh 已配置的模型，无需另外填写 API Key；图像读页需要支持图像输入的模型。"
    },
    {
      "section": "开始使用",
      "text": "1. 在项目会话中上传 PDF，打开右上角「资料库」。\n2. 点击「确认加入并索引」，或从项目文件中选择 PDF。\n3. 勾选本次对话需要查询的文档，直接提问。\n4. 点击回答中的「文档名 · 第 N 页」，在侧栏查看原文与高亮。\n\n插件会向 agent 自动注入引用规则，基于 PDF 的回答默认附可点击来源，无需在问题里额外要求引用。\n\n可以这样问：\n\n> 这份手册的 API 默认设置和变化值是什么？\n\n> 对比两份报告同一年的收入，核对单位。\n\n> 解释图 3 的实验结果，结合正文和邻页说明。"
    },
    {
      "section": "资料库与索引进度",
      "text": "搜索文件名称、切换查看对象，勾选参与检索的文档。展开文件详情可以浏览目录、页码和索引建立过程。\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/library.png\" alt=\"示例手册的资料库、检索范围和索引状态\" width=\"358\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "从回答回到原页",
      "text": "点击引用后，对话旁显示 PDF 原页，支持翻页与缩放。有文字层的引文可高亮定位；扫描页使用页级定位。"
    },
    {
      "section": "数据与模型",
      "text": "PDF 快照和索引保存在本地。摘要、视觉页卡和问答所需的摘录或页面图像会发送到 dsh 当前配置的模型服务，使用该服务的额度。默认资料目录为 `~/.dsh/data/document-evidence`；设置 `DSH_HOME` 后随之调整。"
    },
    {
      "section": "更多",
      "text": "- [配置、工具接口与开发验证](docs/configuration.md)\n- [检索性能与上下文复用测量](docs/optimization-beta8.md)\n- [提交问题](https://github.com/Anduin9527/dsh-document-evidence/issues) · [参与贡献](CONTRIBUTING.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "许可",
      "text": "[AGPL-3.0-only](LICENSE)。依赖说明见 [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)。"
    },
    {
      "section": "Document Library for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Ask questions about your PDFs and follow each citation back to the source page, right inside dsh Web.\n\n[中文](README.md) · [Configuration](docs/configuration.md) · [Changelog](CHANGELOG.md)\n\n*Actual UI capture using a sample manual and a local protocol test model.*"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- A project PDF library shared across sessions, with a separate document selection for each conversation.\n- Background indexing with progress, page coverage, stop and resume controls.\n- Source retrieval, neighboring-page reading and clickable page citations.\n- Page images for charts and scanned content through your existing dsh vision model.\n- Native tool cards showing candidates, excerpts, timing and status."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires dsh Web, Node.js 22.19+ on the 22.x line or 24+, and Python 3.10+ with venv. Verified with `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.3-alpha.2` on macOS arm64.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-document-evidence@beta\ndsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-document-evidence-setup\ndsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Restart dsh if it is already running. Setup creates a dedicated Python environment and installs PyMuPDF. The plugin uses your existing dsh model configuration; no additional API key is needed. Image reading requires a model with image input support."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Upload a PDF in a project conversation and open **资料库** (Library).\n2. Confirm that it should be added and indexed, or choose a project PDF.\n3. Select the documents to search and ask your question.\n4. Click a citation to open the original page and highlight its text.\n\nThe plugin instructs the agent to include clickable sources in PDF-based answers automatically; you do not need to ask for citations.\n\nTry: “Compare revenue for the same year across these two reports. Check the units.”"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "<img src=\"docs/assets/library.png\" alt=\"Sample manual in the document library with index progress\" width=\"358\">\n\nThe library supports filename search, document selection and index progress. Page citations support navigation and zoom; scanned pages use page-level navigation when no text coordinates are available."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data and models",
      "text": "PDF snapshots and indexes stay local. Summaries, visual page cards and answers send the required excerpts or page images to your configured dsh model service and consume its usage. The default data directory is `~/.dsh/data/document-evidence`, or under `DSH_HOME` when set."
    },
    {
      "section": "More",
      "text": "[Configuration and development](docs/configuration.md) · [Performance measurements](docs/optimization-beta8.md) · [Issues](https://github.com/Anduin9527/dsh-document-evidence/issues) · [Contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[AGPL-3.0-only](LICENSE). See [third-party notices](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)."
    }
